// AAC rule-program executor (PLAN-1046 T-02): Auto port of
// `ace_syntax_runtime::parse` — explicit work stacks (no native recursion),
// config-driven Pratt, declaration-level recovery, budgets, failure memo,
// and copy-adopted grafting.
//
// Machine state lives in parallel flat lists threaded through the step
// functions in a FIXED order (the M-tuple):
//   pg, cs, firsts, nullable, toks, t, ef, decls, mc, pending, fr, saves,
//   pvals, pops, optriv, arule, ai, hints, dmsg, fm, ot, oef, odecls,
//   gcand, gshift, ginfo
// (hints are h3=[depth,start,end] stride 3 + hm messages; tree diags
// d3=[start,end] stride 3-2 + dm messages — d3 uses stride 2.)
//
// Disciplines fixed by the lane:
//   * List has no pop — stack-ish lists carry a LOGICAL length in mc;
//   * functions stay small (the AV ownership bound scales blocks × slots);
//   * meta kinds use the signed encoding (-1..-4; the conformance oracle
//     normalizes the Rust canonical form identically);
//   * decl directory: node.decl is the tree-global decl index + 1 (0 =
//     root-level absolute span); origins are decl-relative byte starts.

